patches/generated/kernel-xiaomi-sm8250-ksu-susfs.patch
    Kernel changes: the KernelSU hook integration points in the 4.19 kernel (kernel/sys.c,
    fs/exec.c, fs/open.c, fs/stat.c, kernel/reboot.c, drivers/input/input.c), the SuSFS
    implementation (fs/susfs.c, include/linux/susfs.h, include/linux/susfs_def.h), the
    build wiring, and arch/arm64/configs/vendor/xiaomi/ksu-susfs.config.
    Derived from the Linux kernel 4.19 (GPL-2.0-only) and from SuSFS. The SuSFS files here
    are the in-kernel implementation of SuSFS v2.2.0 (`SUSFS_VERSION` in
    include/linux/susfs_def.h) as carried by the device kernel branch that our integration
    patch came from; that patch credits simonpunk as co-author and points at
    https://github.com/JackA1ltman/NonGKI_Kernel_Build_2nd as the port it followed.
    GPL-2.0-only. Our own lines are licensed so as to keep the result distributable under
    GPL-2.0-only, as the kernel requires. sidex15's repository
    (https://github.com/sidex15/susfs4ksu-module) is the user-space KernelSU module that
    drives this kernel support; it is not the source of the files in this patch.

patches/generated/kernelsu-preinstalled-manager.patch
    A two-file change (kernel/manager/apk_sign.c, kernel/manager/throne_tracker.c) inside
    the BakaSU repository, which published as ReSukiSU at the release this patch was made
    against: it teaches the manager scanner to recognize a manager
    preinstalled in /product/app, and makes the APK-path package parser tolerate a package
    name without a hyphen.
    Derived from BakaSU (https://github.com/Baka-SU/BakaSU), a KernelSU fork; it was published
    as ReSukiSU at v4.2.0-rc1, the release this patch is pinned to. The repository carries a
    GNU GPL v3 LICENSE at its root and a separate GNU GPL v2
    LICENSE inside its `kernel/` directory; both files this patch modifies sit under the
    latter and carry no SPDX header of their own. Treat this patch as GPL-2.0-only and
    consult upstream for the authoritative terms.

